msgstr "Memandangkan masalah mainan ini hanya menggunakan dua qubit, kita boleh semak ini dengan menggunakan penyelesai aljabar linear NumPy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, the result is extremely close to the ideal.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang boleh anda lihat, hasilnya amat hampir dengan nilai ideal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experimenting to improve speed and accuracy {#experimenting-to-improve-speed-and-accuracy}"
msgstr "Bereksperimen untuk meningkatkan kelajuan dan ketepatan {#experimenting-to-improve-speed-and-accuracy}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Add reference state {#add-reference-state}"
msgstr "Tambah keadaan rujukan {#add-reference-state}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the previous example we have not used any reference operator $U_R$. Now let us think about how the ideal eigenstate $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ can be obtained. Consider the following circuit.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh sebelumnya kita tidak menggunakan sebarang operator rujukan $U_R$. Sekarang mari kita fikirkan bagaimana keadaan eigen ideal $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ boleh diperoleh. Pertimbangkan Circuit berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/55b26ae7-ad26-4b54-b4f3-2004bb2db0c9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/55b26ae7-ad26-4b54-b4f3-2004bb2db0c9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can quickly check that this circuit gives us the desired state.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh semak dengan cepat bahawa Circuit ini memberikan keadaan yang kita inginkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have seen how a circuit preparing the solution state looks like, it seems reasonable to use a Hadamard gate as a reference circuit, so that the full ansatz becomes:\n"
msgstr "Sekarang bahawa kita telah melihat rupa bentuk circuit yang menyediakan keadaan penyelesaian, nampaknya munasabah untuk menggunakan gate Hadamard sebagai circuit rujukan, supaya ansatz penuh menjadi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/14e04c7a-e81f-41e1-b0cf-790954581be9-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/14e04c7a-e81f-41e1-b0cf-790954581be9-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this new circuit, the ideal solution could be reached with all the parameters set to $0$, so this confirms that the choice of reference circuit is reasonable.\n"
msgstr "Untuk circuit baru ini, penyelesaian ideal boleh dicapai apabila semua parameter ditetapkan kepada $0$, jadi ini mengesahkan bahawa pilihan circuit rujukan adalah munasabah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let us compare the number of cost function evaluations, optimizer iterations and time taken with those of the previous attempt.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita bandingkan bilangan penilaian fungsi kos, iterasi pengoptimum dan masa yang diambil berbanding percubaan sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Using our optimal parameters to calculate the minimum eigenvalue:\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan parameter optimum kita untuk mengira nilai eigen minimum:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Depending on your specific system, this may or may not result in an improvement in speed or accuracy in this very small scale example. The point is that starting with physically-motivated reference states becomes increasingly important in improving speed and accuracy as problems scale.\n"
msgstr "Bergantung pada sistem tertentu anda, ini mungkin atau mungkin tidak menghasilkan peningkatan dalam kelajuan atau ketepatan pada contoh berskala sangat kecil ini. Yang penting ialah bermula dengan keadaan rujukan yang bermotivasi secara fizikal menjadi semakin penting dalam meningkatkan kelajuan dan ketepatan apabila masalah berskala lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change the initial point {#change-the-initial-point}"
msgstr "Tukar titik awal {#change-the-initial-point}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have seen the effect of adding the reference state, we will go into what happens when we choose different initial points $\\vec{\\theta_0}$. In particular we will use $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ and $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang bahawa kita telah melihat kesan penambahan keadaan rujukan, kita akan lihat apa yang berlaku apabila kita memilih titik awal $\\vec{\\theta_0}$ yang berbeza. Khususnya kita akan menggunakan $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(0,0,0,0,6,0,0,0)$ dan $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that, as discussed when the reference state was introduced, the ideal solution would be found when all the parameters are $0$, so the first initial point should give fewer evaluations.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa, seperti yang dibincangkan ketika keadaan rujukan diperkenalkan, penyelesaian ideal akan ditemui apabila semua parameter adalah $0$, jadi titik awal pertama sepatutnya memberikan lebih sedikit penilaian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adjusting initial point to $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"
msgstr "Melaraskan titik awal kepada $\\vec{\\theta_0}=(6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6,6)$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By experimenting with different initial points, you might be able to achieve convergence faster and with fewer function evaluations.\n"
msgstr "Dengan bereksperimen menggunakan titik awal yang berbeza, anda mungkin boleh mencapai penumpuan lebih cepat dengan lebih sedikit penilaian fungsi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Experimenting with different optimizers {#experimenting-with-different-optimizers}"
msgstr "Bereksperimen dengan pengoptimum yang berbeza {#experimenting-with-different-optimizers}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can adjust the optimizer using SciPy `minimize`'s `method` argument, with more options [found here](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html). We originally used a constrained minimizer (`COBYLA`). In this example, we'll explore using an unconstrained minimizer (`BFGS`) instead\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh melaraskan pengoptimum menggunakan argumen `method` dalam `minimize` SciPy, dengan lebih banyak pilihan [yang boleh ditemui di sini](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.optimize.minimize.html). Asalnya kita menggunakan pengecil tertakhluk (`COBYLA`). Dalam contoh ini, kita akan terokai menggunakan pengecil tidak tertakhlud (`BFGS`) sebagai ganti\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "VQD example {#vqd-example}"
msgstr "Contoh VQD {#vqd-example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we implement the Qiskit patterns framework, explicitly.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita melaksanakan rangka kerja corak Qiskit secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasikal kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now instead of looking for only the lowest eigenvalue of our observables, we will look for all $4$, (where $k=4$).\n"
msgstr "Kini, bukannya mencari hanya nilai eigen terendah bagi observable kita, kita akan mencari kesemua $4$, (di mana $k=4$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remember that the cost functions of VQD are:\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa fungsi kos VQD ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"C_{l}(\\vec{\\theta}) :=\n"
"\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) | \\hat{H} | \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})\\rangle +\n"
"\\sum_{j=0}^{l-1}\\beta_j |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2\n"
"\\quad \\forall l\\in\\{1,\\cdots,k\\}=\\{1,\\cdots,4\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is particularly important because a vector $\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (in this case $(\\beta_0, \\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) must be passed as an argument when we define the `VQD` object.\n"
msgstr "Ini amat penting kerana vektor $\\vec{\\beta}=(\\beta_0,\\cdots,\\beta_{k-1})$ (dalam kes ini $(\\beta_0, \\beta_1, \\beta_2, \\beta_3)$) mesti dihantar sebagai argumen apabila kita mendefinisikan objek `VQD`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Also, in Qiskit's implementation of VQD, instead of considering the effective observables described in the previous notebook, the fidelities $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ are calculated directly via the `ComputeUncompute` algorithm, that leverages a `Sampler` primitive to sample the probability of obtaining $|0\\rangle$ for the circuit\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. This works precisely because this probability is\n"
msgstr ""
"Juga, dalam implementasi VQD Qiskit, berbanding menggunakan observable efektif yang diterangkan dalam notebook sebelumnya, kesetiaan $|\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta})| \\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j})\\rangle  |^2$ dikira secara langsung melalui algoritma `ComputeUncompute`, yang memanfaatkan primitif `Sampler` untuk mensampel kebarangkalian memperoleh $|0\\rangle$ bagi Circuit\n"
"$U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})$. Ini berfungsi tepat kerana kebarangkalian ini ialah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "p_0\n"
msgstr "p_0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\big(\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\big(\\langle 0|U_A^\\dagger(\\vec{\\theta})\\big)\\big(U_A(\\vec{\\theta^j})|0\\rangle\\big)|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = |\\langle \\psi(\\vec{\\theta}) |\\psi(\\vec{\\theta^j}) \\rangle|^2 \\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/e4d59381-43ff-4322-a6f2-df55cef18536-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/e4d59381-43ff-4322-a6f2-df55cef18536-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's start by examining the following observable:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita mulakan dengan memeriksa observable berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 := 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 := 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\lambda_0 = -7 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_1 = 3\\\\\n"
"\\lambda_2 = 5 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_3 = 7\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"\\lambda_0 = -7 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_1 = 3\\\\\n"
"\\lambda_2 = 5 \\\\\n"
"\\lambda_3 = 7\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle + |10\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\left\\{\n"
"\\begin{array}{c}\n"
"|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle - |11\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle + |10\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle)\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"\\right\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll be using the following function to calculate the overlap penalty. Note that this is still part of mapping the problem to quantum circuits. However, as discussed in the previous lesson, this function calculates the overlap between a current variational circuit and the optimized circuit from a previous, lower-energy/cost state obtained. The new circuit being generated also has to be transpiled to run on real hardware. We have seen this function before, used on a simulator. Here, we must already consider the transpiling and related optimization for when we use a real backend, hence the lines around `if realbackend == 1`. This is mixing a bit of step 2, but we will call out step 2 explicitly later.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan fungsi berikut untuk mengira penalti pertindihan. Perhatikan bahawa ini masih sebahagian daripada pemetaan masalah kepada Circuit kuantum. Namun, seperti yang dibincangkan dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, fungsi ini mengira pertindihan antara Circuit variasi semasa dan Circuit yang telah dioptimumkan daripada keadaan tenaga/kos lebih rendah yang diperoleh sebelumnya. Circuit baharu yang dijana juga perlu ditranspil untuk dijalankan pada perkakasan sebenar. Kita telah melihat fungsi ini sebelum ini, digunakan pada simulator. Di sini, kita perlu sudah mempertimbangkan transpilasi dan pengoptimuman berkaitan untuk apabila kita menggunakan Backend sebenar, oleh itu baris di sekitar `if realbackend == 1`. Ini sedikit mencampurkan langkah 2, tetapi kita akan menyebut langkah 2 secara eksplisit kemudian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we add VQD's cost function. Note that compared to the previous lesson, we now have two additional arguments (`realbackend` and `backend`) to help us with transpilation when we use real backends.\n"
msgstr "Kini kita tambahkan fungsi kos VQD. Perhatikan bahawa berbanding pelajaran sebelumnya, kita kini mempunyai dua argumen tambahan (`realbackend` dan `backend`) untuk membantu kita dengan transpilasi apabila menggunakan Backend sebenar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Once again, we will use simulators for debugging, and then move on to real hardware.\n"
msgstr "Sekali lagi, kita akan menggunakan simulator untuk nyahpepijat, kemudian beralih ke perkakasan sebenar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we introduce the number of states we wish to calculate, the penalties, and a set of initial parameters, x0.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita memperkenalkan bilangan keadaan yang ingin dikira, penalti, dan satu set parameter awal, x0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now test the algorithm using simulators:\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menguji algoritma menggunakan simulator sekarang:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These results are fairly close to the expected ones except for approximation error and global phase. We could adjust the tolerance on the classical optimizer and/or the penalties for statevector overlap to obtain more precise values.\n"
msgstr "Keputusan ini agak hampir dengan yang dijangkakan kecuali untuk ralat anggaran dan fasa global. Kita boleh menyesuaikan toleransi pada pengoptimum klasikal dan/atau penalti pertindihan keadaan vektor untuk mendapatkan nilai yang lebih tepat.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Change betas {#change-betas}"
msgstr "Tukar beta {#change-betas}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As mentioned in the previous lesson, the values of $\\vec{\\beta}$ should be bigger than the difference between eigenvalues. Let us see what happens when they do not satisfy that condition with $\\hat{O}_2$\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang disebutkan dalam pelajaran sebelumnya, nilai $\\vec{\\beta}$ seharusnya lebih besar daripada perbezaan antara nilai eigen. Mari kita lihat apa yang berlaku apabila syarat itu tidak dipenuhi dengan $\\hat{O}_2$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 = 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{O}_2 = 2 II - 3 XX + 2 YY - 4 ZZ\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with eigenvalues\n"
msgstr "dengan nilai eigen\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This time, the optimizer returns the same state $|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ as a proposed solution to all eigenstates: which is clearly wrong. This happens because the betas were too small to penalize the minimum eigenstate in the successive cost functions. Therefore, it was not excluded from the effective search space in later iterations of the algorithm, and always chosen as the best possible solution.\n"
msgstr "Kali ini, pengoptimum mengembalikan keadaan yang sama $|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|00\\rangle + |11\\rangle)$ sebagai penyelesaian cadangan untuk semua keadaan eigen: yang jelas salah. Ini berlaku kerana nilai beta terlalu kecil untuk menghukum keadaan eigen minimum dalam fungsi kos berturutan. Oleh itu, ia tidak dikecualikan daripada ruang carian efektif dalam iterasi algoritma seterusnya, dan sentiasa dipilih sebagai penyelesaian terbaik yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recommend experimenting with the values of $\\vec{\\beta}$, and ensuring they are bigger than the difference between eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr "Kita mengesyorkan untuk bereksperimen dengan nilai $\\vec{\\beta}$, dan memastikan ia lebih besar daripada perbezaan antara nilai eigen.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan masalah untuk pelaksanaan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-execution}"

# doq-bootstrap: msgid repeated on page, first translation kept
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To run this on real hardware, we must optimize the quantum circuits for our quantum computer of choice. For our purposes here, we will simply use the least busy backend.\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjalankan ini pada perkakasan sebenar, kita perlu mengoptimumkan Circuit kuantum untuk komputer kuantum pilihan kita. Untuk tujuan kita di sini, kita akan menggunakan Backend yang paling kurang sibuk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will transpile our circuit using a preset pass manager and optimization level 3.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mentranspil Circuit kita menggunakan pengurus laluan prasetel dengan tahap pengoptimuman 3.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using IBM Quantum primitives {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif IBM Quantum {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Taking care to reset our betas to sufficiently high values, we can now run our calculation on real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Dengan memastikan nilai beta kita ditetapkan semula kepada nilai yang cukup tinggi, kita kini boleh menjalankan pengiraan kita pada perkakasan kuantum sebenar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process, return result in classical format {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses, kembalikan keputusan dalam format klasikal {#step-4-post-process-return-result-in-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our output is structurally similar to what has been discussed in previous lessons and examples. But there is something problematic in the results above, from which we can derive a cautionary message for the context of excited states. To limit computing time used on this learning example, we set a maximum number of iterations for classical optimizer that was potentially too low: 200 iterations. A previous calculation above, on a simulator, failed to converge in 200 iterations. Here, ours did converge... but to what tolerance? We have not specified a tolerance for COBYLA to consider itself \"converged\". A glance at the function value and comparison with previous runs tells us that COBYLA was not close to converging to the precision we require.\n"
msgstr "Output kita secara strukturnya serupa dengan apa yang telah dibincangkan dalam pelajaran dan contoh sebelumnya. Tetapi ada sesuatu yang bermasalah dalam keputusan di atas, dari mana kita boleh mengambil peringatan penting dalam konteks keadaan teruja. Untuk mengehadkan masa pengiraan yang digunakan dalam contoh pembelajaran ini, kita menetapkan bilangan iterasi maksimum untuk pengoptimum klasikal yang berpotensi terlalu rendah: 200 iterasi. Pengiraan sebelumnya di atas, pada simulator, gagal menumpu dalam 200 iterasi. Di sini, kita memang menumpu... tetapi kepada toleransi yang mana? Kita tidak menentukan toleransi untuk COBYLA menganggap dirinya \"menumpu\". Sepintas lalu pada nilai fungsi dan perbandingan dengan jalankan sebelumnya memberitahu kita bahawa COBYLA tidak hampir menumpu kepada ketepatan yang kita perlukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is another issue: the energy of the first excited state appears to be lower than the energy of the ground state! See if you can explain how this could happen. Hint: it is related to the convergence point we just addressed. This behavior is explained in detail below after VQD is applied to the H2 molecule.\n"
msgstr "Ada isu lain: tenaga keadaan teruja pertama kelihatan lebih rendah daripada tenaga keadaan asas! Cuba jelaskan bagaimana ini boleh berlaku. Petunjuk: ia berkaitan dengan titik penumpuan yang baru kita bincangkan. Tingkah laku ini diterangkan secara terperinci di bawah selepas VQD diaplikasikan pada molekul H2.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum chemistry: ground state and excited energy solver {#quantum-chemistry-ground-state-and-excited-energy-solver}"
msgstr "Kimia kuantum: penyelesai tenaga keadaan asas dan teruja {#quantum-chemistry-ground-state-and-excited-energy-solver}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our objective is to minimize the expectation value of the observable representing energy (Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"
msgstr "Objektif kita adalah untuk meminimumkan nilai jangkaan bagi observable yang mewakili tenaga (Hamiltonian $\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}$):\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\min_{\\vec\\theta} \\langle\\psi(\\vec\\theta)|\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}|\\psi(\\vec\\theta)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/de006d72-db04-49d4-806b-89bd1e5b9947-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/de006d72-db04-49d4-806b-89bd1e5b9947-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can minimize this cost function to calculate optimal parameters, and we can check our code first by using a local simulator.\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh meminimumkan fungsi kos ini untuk mengira parameter optimum, dan kita boleh semak kod kita dahulu menggunakan simulator tempatan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The minimum value of the cost function (-1.857...) is the ground state energy of the H2 molecule, in units of hartrees.\n"
msgstr "Nilai minimum fungsi kos (-1.857...) ialah tenaga keadaan asas molekul H2, dalam unit hartree.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Excited States {#excited-states}"
msgstr "Keadaan Teruja {#excited-states}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can also leverage VQD to solve for $k=2$ total states (the ground state and the first excited state).\n"
msgstr "Kita juga boleh menggunakan VQD untuk menyelesaikan $k=2$ keadaan jumlah (keadaan asas dan keadaan teruja pertama).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll add our overlap calculation:\n"
msgstr "Kita akan tambah pengiraan pertindihan:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real hardware and a final cautionary message {#real-hardware-and-a-final-cautionary-message}"
msgstr "Perkakasan sebenar dan pesanan berhati-hati {#real-hardware-and-a-final-cautionary-message}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will use a preset pass manager for transpilation, and we will maximally optimize our circuit using optimization level 3.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan menggunakan pengurus laluan pratetap untuk transpilasi, dan kita akan mengoptimumkan Circuit kita secara maksimum menggunakan tahap pengoptimuman 3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because VQD is highly iterative, we will carry out all steps inside a Runtime session, such that our jobs will only be queued at the beginning, and not between every parameter update. Nothing else changes about the syntax for the cost function or estimator.\n"
msgstr "Kerana VQD sangat berulang, kita akan menjalankan semua langkah dalam satu Runtime Session, supaya kerja-kerja kita hanya diantrekan pada awal sahaja, bukan di antara setiap kemas kini parameter. Tiada perkara lain yang berubah mengenai sintaks fungsi kos atau Estimator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The ground state energy obtained (-1.83 hartrees) is not too far from the correct value (-1.85 hartrees). However, the excited state energy is quite a bit off. This is similar to the erroneous behavior we saw earlier in this lesson. The energy reported for the excited state is nearly the same as that for the ground state. In the previous case, we even saw an excited state energy that was _lower_ than the reported ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "Tenaga keadaan asas yang diperoleh (-1.83 hartree) tidak terlalu jauh daripada nilai yang betul (-1.85 hartree). Namun, tenaga keadaan teruja agak berbeza. Ini serupa dengan tingkah laku yang salah yang kita lihat sebelum ini dalam pelajaran ini. Tenaga yang dilaporkan untuk keadaan teruja hampir sama dengan keadaan asas. Dalam kes sebelumnya, kita malah melihat tenaga keadaan teruja yang _lebih rendah_ daripada tenaga keadaan asas yang dilaporkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is not possible for a variational calculation to yield an energy that is lower than the true ground state energy. In the earlier instance, the ground state energy we obtained was not very close to the true ground state. Since we did not obtain the true ground state energy in that case, there is no contradiction. In the present case, the ground state energy was fairly close to the correct value, and yet the excited state energy seems strangely close to that same value.\n"
msgstr "Tidak mungkin pengiraan variasional menghasilkan tenaga yang lebih rendah daripada tenaga keadaan asas sebenar. Dalam kes terdahulu, tenaga keadaan asas yang kita peroleh tidak begitu hampir dengan keadaan asas sebenar. Kerana kita tidak mendapat tenaga keadaan asas yang benar dalam kes itu, tiada percanggahan. Dalam kes semasa, tenaga keadaan asas agak hampir dengan nilai yang betul, namun tenaga keadaan teruja nampaknya anehnya hampir dengan nilai yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To understand better how this happened, recall that the way we find an excited state is by requiring that the variational state be orthogonal to the ground state (using the overlap circuits and penalty terms). If we fail to obtain an accurate ground state energy (or are off by a few percent), then we also fail to obtain an accurate ground state vector! So when we require that the excited state be orthogonal to the first state we found, we were not imposing orthogonality with the true ground state, but rather with some approximation of it (sometimes a poor approximation of it). Thus, the excited state was not forced to be orthogonal to the true ground state, and our energy estimates for the excited states were actually quite close to the ground state energy.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memahami dengan lebih baik bagaimana ini berlaku, ingat bahawa cara kita mencari keadaan teruja ialah dengan mensyaratkan bahawa keadaan variasional berortogon dengan keadaan asas (menggunakan Circuit pertindihan dan sebutan penalti). Jika kita gagal mendapatkan tenaga keadaan asas yang tepat (atau tersasar beberapa peratus), maka kita juga gagal mendapatkan vektor keadaan asas yang tepat! Jadi apabila kita mensyaratkan bahawa keadaan teruja berortogon dengan keadaan pertama yang kita temui, kita tidak mengenakan ortogonaliti dengan keadaan asas sebenar, sebaliknya dengan suatu penghampiran (kadang-kadang penghampiran yang kurang tepat). Oleh itu, keadaan teruja tidak dipaksa untuk berortogon dengan keadaan asas sebenar, dan anggaran tenaga bagi keadaan teruja kita sebenarnya agak hampir dengan tenaga keadaan asas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This will always be a concern in VQD. But in principle, this can be corrected by increasing the maximum number of iterations for the classical optimizer, imposing lower tolerance for the classical optimizer, and possibly also trying a different ansatz if we are habitually missing the true ground state. As we have seen, one may also need to modify the overlap penalties (betas). But that is really a separate issue. No penalty for overlap will keep you away from the true ground state, if you haven't found a very good estimate of the true ground state for the overlap circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ini akan sentiasa menjadi kebimbangan dalam VQD. Namun pada dasarnya, ini boleh diperbetulkan dengan meningkatkan bilangan maksimum lelaran untuk pengoptimum klasik, mengenakan toleransi yang lebih rendah untuk pengoptimum klasik, dan mungkin juga mencuba ansatz yang berbeza jika kita selalu terlepas keadaan asas sebenar. Seperti yang kita lihat, mungkin juga perlu mengubah suai penalti pertindihan (betas). Namun itu sebenarnya isu yang berasingan. Tiada penalti untuk pertindihan yang akan menjauhkan anda daripada keadaan asas sebenar, jika anda belum menemui anggaran yang sangat baik bagi keadaan asas sebenar untuk Circuit pertindihan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Optimization: max-cut {#optimization-max-cut}"
msgstr "Pengoptimuman: Max-Cut {#optimization-max-cut}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum cut (max-cut) problem is a combinatorial optimization problem that involves dividing the vertices of a graph into two disjoint sets such that the number of edges between the two sets is maximized. More formally, given an undirected graph $G=(V,E)$, where $V$ is the set of vertices and $E$ is the set of edges, the max-cut problem asks to partition the vertices into two disjoint subsets, $S$ and $T$, such that the number of edges with one endpoint in $S$ and the other in $T$ is maximized.\n"
msgstr "Masalah potongan maksimum (Max-Cut) ialah masalah pengoptimuman kombinatori yang melibatkan pembahagian bucu graf kepada dua set yang tidak bertindih supaya bilangan tepi antara dua set itu dimaksimumkan. Secara lebih formal, diberi graf tidak terarah $G=(V,E)$, di mana $V$ ialah set bucu dan $E$ ialah set tepi, masalah Max-Cut meminta kita membahagikan bucu kepada dua subset yang tidak bertindih, $S$ dan $T$, supaya bilangan tepi dengan satu hujung dalam $S$ dan hujung lain dalam $T$ dimaksimumkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can apply max-cut to solve a various problems, such as clustering, network design, and phase transitions. We'll start by creating a problem graph:\n"
msgstr "Kita boleh menggunakan Max-Cut untuk menyelesaikan pelbagai masalah, seperti pengelompokan, reka bentuk rangkaian, dan peralihan fasa. Mari kita mulakan dengan mencipta graf masalah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/3eb71b79-a988-4807-aa88-7fb25a78a236-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This problem can be expressed as a binary optimization problem. For each node $0 \\leq i < n$, where $n$ is the number of nodes of the graph (in this case $n=4$), we will consider the binary variable $x_i$. This variable will have the value $1$ if node $i$ is one of the groups that we'll label $1$ and $0$ if it's in the other group, that we'll label as $0$. We will also denote as $w_{ij}$ (element $(i,j)$ of the adjacency matrix $w$) the weight of the edge that goes from node $i$ to node $j$. Because the graph is undirected, $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$. Then we can formulate our problem as maximizing the following cost function:\n"
msgstr "Masalah ini boleh dinyatakan sebagai masalah pengoptimuman binari. Bagi setiap nod $0 \\leq i < n$, di mana $n$ ialah bilangan nod graf (dalam kes ini $n=4$), kita akan mempertimbangkan pemboleh ubah binari $x_i$. Pemboleh ubah ini akan bernilai $1$ jika nod $i$ berada dalam salah satu kumpulan yang akan kita labelkan sebagai $1$, dan $0$ jika berada dalam kumpulan lain yang akan kita labelkan sebagai $0$. Kita juga akan menandakan $w_{ij}$ (elemen $(i,j)$ matriks bersebelahan $w$) sebagai berat tepi yang menghubungkan nod $i$ ke nod $j$. Kerana graf ini tidak terarah, $w_{ij}=w_{ji}$. Kemudian kita boleh merumuskan masalah kita sebagai memaksimumkan fungsi kos berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{x})\n"
"& =\\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i(1-x_j)\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_ix_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} x_i - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i 2w_{ij} x_ix_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To solve this problem with a quantum computer, we are going to express the cost function as the expected value of an observable. However, the observables that Qiskit admits natively consist of Pauli operators, that have eigenvalues $1$ and $-1$ instead of $0$ and $1$. That's why we are going to make the following change of variable:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menyelesaikan masalah ini dengan komputer kuantum, kita akan menyatakan fungsi kos sebagai nilai jangkaan suatu boleh cerapan. Walau bagaimanapun, boleh cerapan yang Qiskit sokong secara asli terdiri daripada operator Pauli, yang mempunyai nilai eigen $1$ dan $-1$ berbanding $0$ dan $1$. Sebab itulah kita akan membuat perubahan pemboleh ubah berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$. We can use the adjacency matrix $w$ to comfortably access the weights of all the edge. This will be used to obtain our cost function:\n"
msgstr "Di mana $\\vec{x}=(x_0,x_1,\\cdots ,x_{n-1})$. Kita boleh menggunakan matriks bersebelahan $w$ untuk mengakses berat semua tepi dengan mudah. Ini akan digunakan untuk mendapatkan fungsi kos kita:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i = 1-2x_i \\rightarrow x_i = \\frac{1-z_i}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This implies that:\n"
msgstr "Ini bermakna:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{lcl} x_i=0 & \\rightarrow & z_i=1 \\\\ x_i=1 & \\rightarrow & z_i=-1.\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "So the new cost function we want to maximize is:\n"
msgstr "Jadi fungsi kos baru yang ingin kita maksimumkan ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"C(\\vec{z})\n"
"& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n w_{ij} \\bigg(\\frac{1-z_i}{2}\\bigg)\\bigg(1-\\frac{1-z_j}{2}\\bigg)\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"
msgstr "& = \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} - \\sum_{i,j=0}^n \\frac{w_{ij}}{4} z_iz_j\\\\[1mm]\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"& = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Moreover, the natural tendency of a quantum computer is to find minima (usually the lowest energy) instead of maxima so instead of maximizing $C(\\vec{z})$ we are going to minimize:\n"
msgstr "Selain itu, kecenderungan semula jadi komputer kuantum adalah untuk mencari minimum (biasanya tenaga terendah) bukan maksimum, jadi sebagai ganti memaksimumkan $C(\\vec{z})$, kita akan meminimumkan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"-C(\\vec{z}) =  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} z_iz_j -  \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now that we have a cost function to minimize whose variables can have the values $-1$ and $1$, we can make the following analogy with the Pauli $Z$:\n"
msgstr "Kini setelah kita mempunyai fungsi kos untuk diminimumkan yang pemboleh ubahnya boleh mempunyai nilai $-1$ dan $1$, kita boleh membuat analogi berikut dengan Pauli $Z$:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"z_i \\equiv Z_i = \\overbrace{I}^{n-1}\\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{Z}^{i} \\otimes ... \\otimes \\overbrace{I}^{0}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In other words, the variable $z_i$ will be equivalent to a $Z$ gate acting on qubit $i$. Moreover:\n"
msgstr "Dengan kata lain, pemboleh ubah $z_i$ akan bersamaan dengan gate $Z$ yang bertindak pada qubit $i$. Selain itu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle \\rightarrow \\langle x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0 |Z_i|x_{n-1}\\cdots x_0\\rangle = z_i\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then the observable we are going to consider is:\n"
msgstr "Kemudian boleh cerapan yang akan kita pertimbangkan ialah:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2} Z_iZ_j\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "to which we will have to add the independent term afterwards:\n"
msgstr "yang mana kita perlu menambah sebutan bebas selepas itu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"The operator is a linear combination of terms with Z operators on nodes connected by an edge (recall that the 0th qubit is farthest right): $IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$. Once the operator is constructed, the ansatz for the QAOA algorithm can easily be built by using the `QAOAAnsatz` circuit from the Qiskit circuit library.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\texttt{offset} = - \\sum_{i=0}^n \\sum_{j=0}^i \\frac{w_{ij}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
"Operator ini ialah gabungan linear sebutan dengan operator Z pada nod yang dihubungkan oleh tepi (ingat bahawa qubit ke-0 paling jauh di kanan): $IIZZ + IZIZ + IZZI + ZIIZ + ZZII$. Setelah operator dibina, ansatz untuk algoritma QAOA boleh dibina dengan mudah menggunakan Circuit `QAOAAnsatz` dari pustaka Circuit Qiskit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/variational-algorithm-design/examples-and-applications/extracted-outputs/d28c4262-a080-4fe4-9427-762326184cd8-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now set an initial set of random parameters:\n"
msgstr "Kita kini menetapkan set awal parameter rawak:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any classical optimizer can be used to minimize the cost function. On a real quantum system, an optimizer designed for non-smooth cost function landscapes usually does better. Here we use the [COBYLA routine](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) from SciPy via the minimize function.\n"
msgstr "Mana-mana pengoptimum klasik boleh digunakan untuk meminimumkan fungsi kos. Pada sistem kuantum sebenar, pengoptimum yang direka bentuk untuk landskap fungsi kos yang tidak licin biasanya lebih baik. Di sini kita menggunakan [rutin COBYLA](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/optimize.minimize-cobyla.html#optimize-minimize-cobyla) dari SciPy melalui fungsi minimize.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because we are iteratively executing many calls to Runtime, we make use of a session to execute all calls within a single block. Moreover, for QAOA, the solution is encoded in the output distribution of the ansatz circuit bound with the optimal parameters from the minimization. Therefore, we will need a Sampler primitive, and will instantiate it with the same session\n"
"And run our minimization routine:\n"
msgstr "Kerana kita melaksanakan banyak panggilan ke Runtime secara berulang, kita menggunakan Session untuk melaksanakan semua panggilan dalam satu blok. Selain itu, untuk QAOA, penyelesaian dikodkan dalam taburan output Circuit ansatz yang diikat dengan parameter optimum hasil minimisasi. Oleh itu, kita akan memerlukan primitif Sampler, dan akan membuat instantnya dengan Session yang sama. Kemudian jalankan rutin minimisasi kita:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The solution vector of parameter angles (`x`), when plugged into the ansatz circuit, yields the graph partitioning that we were looking for.\n"
msgstr "Vektor penyelesaian sudut parameter (`x`), apabila dimasukkan ke dalam Circuit ansatz, menghasilkan pembahagian graf yang kita cari.\n"

